; ==========================================================================
; Bouncing-Ball-v06  -  two 3x3 balls that bounce off each other, faster again
; ==========================================================================
; v05 made faster: the same balls, bounces and collision latch. Measured in the
; simulator on V0061.34 (Firmware-Math/ball5_verify.py --v05):
;
;   v06: 17,146 1802 instructions and 109 serial bytes a frame; v05: 25,919 and 134 - v06 is 1.51x faster
;
; WHERE v05's TIME WENT. Over half of a frame was cursor moves and strings: each
; ball made up to three cursor moves a frame (14 commands each) - blank its stale
; column, blank its stale row when it moved up or down, then draw all nine cells.
; v06 makes ONE cursor move a ball, to the top-left of the box its old and new
; places cover, and ONE PRINTSTR of a string made for that move (right or left,
; and up, level or down: six strings): the cells it left are blanked, the cells it
; came to are lit, the cells it keeps are not touched. ESC[A, ESC[nC and ESC[nD
; join ESC[B for the moves inside a string.
; When the balls are close (under 5 apart both ways) one ball's erase could touch
; the other, so both are then drawn whole, as v05 drew them every frame.
; The frame delay is DLYI 01 (v05: DLYI 04).
;
; REGISTERS. R0 the frame phase 0-5, R1-R5 ball A and R6-R10 ball B as x, y,
; x-direction, y-direction and the ball's row in the phase table (angle x 6),
; R11/R12 old x/y, R13 line and R14 column for POSXY, R15 a pointer.
; Data at $4900 past the end marker: banner, the latch ($4950), the phase
; table ($4960), the digit tables ($4980, $49E0) and the strings ($4A40).
;
; Built by Firmware-Math/build_ball6.py; checked by Firmware-Math/ball5_verify.py
; (the screen is exactly the two balls after every frame, five launches).
; Any key launches, ESC stops and tidies up.
;
; v05 HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-26. v06: not yet on hardware.
; VERSION:  06
;
; 297 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4320 (801 bytes of code).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                      Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 09 00    LOADXI R15 0900            Point at the banner
; D 4005 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Print it
; SEED:
; D 4007 C3             RAND                       Advance the generator - the count depends on the operator
; D 4008 CC             SERST                      Has a key arrived?
; D 4009 A1 00 07       IFFALSEI SEED              Not yet - go round again
; D 400C CB             SERIN                      Take the key and throw it away
; D 400D 51 00 00       SUBXYZ R0 - R0 -> R0       Frame phase, 0-5, starts at 0
; D 4010 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            The touching latch starts clear
; D 4014 32 0F 00 00    COPYMX2I R15 0000
; D 4018 11 01 00 22    LOADXI R1 0022             Ball A starts at column 34
; D 401C 11 02 00 0F    LOADXI R2 000F             line 15
; D 4020 11 06 00 2C    LOADXI R6 002C             Ball B starts at column 44
; D 4024 11 07 00 05    LOADXI R7 0005             and line 5
; D 4028 C3             RAND                       One random value drives both launches
; D 4029 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11          Park it in R11
; D 402B 11 0C 00 02    LOADXI R12 0002            Two
; D 402F 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4031 27             COPYREMA
; D 4032 21 03          COPYAX Acc -> R3           Ball A horizontal direction
; D 4034 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4035 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4037 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4039 27             COPYREMA
; D 403A 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4           Ball A vertical direction
; D 403C 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 403D 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 403F 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4041 27             COPYREMA
; D 4042 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8           Ball B horizontal direction
; D 4044 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4045 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4047 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4049 27             COPYREMA
; D 404A 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9           Ball B vertical direction
; D 404C 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 404D 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 404F 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003            Three
; D 4053 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4055 27             COPYREMA
; D 4056 21 05          COPYAX Acc -> R5           Ball A angle, 0-2
; D 4058 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4059 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 405B 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 405D 27             COPYREMA
; D 405E 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10          Ball B angle, 0-2
; D 4060 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4061 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4063 50 55 0F       ADDXYZ R5 + R5 -> R15      Ball A: its row in the phase table is angle x 6
; D 4066 50 F5 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R5 -> R15
; D 4069 50 FF 05       ADDXYZ R15 + R15 -> R5
; D 406C 50 AA 0F       ADDXYZ R10 + R10 -> R15    Ball B: its row in the phase table is angle x 6
; D 406F 50 FA 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R10 -> R15
; D 4072 50 FF 0A       ADDXYZ R15 + R15 -> R10
; D 4075 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4077 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4079 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 407B CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A 'J'             J - clear the screen
; D 407D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 407F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4081 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F '?'             ?
; D 4083 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 4085 CA 35          SEROUTI 35 '5'             5
; D 4087 CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C 'l'             l - hide the cursor
; D 4089 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 -> R14
; D 408C 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 408F BD 02 DB       CALL DRAW                  Put ball A on the screen
; D 4092 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 -> R14
; D 4095 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 4098 BD 02 DB       CALL DRAW                  and ball B
; LOOP:
; D 409B 42 00          INCX R0                    Next frame phase
; D 409D 86 00 00 06    TESTXI R0 0006
; D 40A1 A1 00 A8       IFFALSEI PH
; D 40A4 53 00 00 06    SUBXI R0 0006              wrapping 5 -> 0
; PH:
; D 40A8 45 16          SUBXY R1 - R6              How far apart horizontally?
; D 40AA 25             COPYMAA                    The magnitude
; D 40AB 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 40AD 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003            Three - the ball's width
; D 40B1 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12          Under three?
; D 40B3 A1 00 E9       IFFALSEI NOHIT             No - clear of each other
; D 40B6 45 27          SUBXY R2 - R7              How far apart vertically?
; D 40B8 25             COPYMAA                    The magnitude
; D 40B9 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 40BB 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12          Under three?
; D 40BD A1 00 E9       IFFALSEI NOHIT             No - clear vertically, so no collision
; D 40C0 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            Point at the touching latch
; D 40C4 33 0F          COPYMXA 0F                 Read it
; D 40C6 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000                Were they apart last frame?
; D 40C9 A1 00 DE       IFFALSEI LATCH             No - already bounced, leave them alone
; D 40CC 23 00 3B       COPYXY R3 -> R11           Save ball A's horizontal direction
; D 40CF 23 00 83       COPYXY R8 -> R3            Ball A takes ball B's
; D 40D2 23 00 B8       COPYXY R11 -> R8           and ball B takes ball A's
; D 40D5 23 00 4B       COPYXY R4 -> R11           The same for the vertical directions
; D 40D8 23 00 94       COPYXY R9 -> R4
; D 40DB 23 00 B9       COPYXY R11 -> R9
; LATCH:
; D 40DE 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            Remember that they are touching
; D 40E2 32 0F 00 01    COPYMX2I R15 0001
; D 40E6 B0 00 F1       GAL HITDONE
; NOHIT:
; D 40E9 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            They are apart - clear the latch
; D 40ED 32 0F 00 00    COPYMX2I R15 0000
; HITDONE:
; D 40F1 23 00 1B       COPYXY R1 -> R11           Remember where this ball is
; D 40F4 23 00 2C       COPYXY R2 -> R12
; D 40F7 86 03 00 00    TESTXI R3 0000             Heading right?
; D 40FB A1 01 12       IFFALSEI XLA               No - heading left
; D 40FE 42 01          INCX R1                    x = x + 1
; D 4100 86 01 00 4E    TESTXI R1 004E             Would the right edge pass column 79?
; D 4104 A1 01 23       IFFALSEI XDA               No - carry on
; D 4107 11 01 00 4C    LOADXI R1 004C             Reflect to 76
; D 410B 11 03 00 01    LOADXI R3 0001             and bounce - now heading left
; D 410F B0 01 23       GAL XDA
; XLA:
; D 4112 43 01          DECX R1                    x = x - 1
; D 4114 86 01 00 01    TESTXI R1 0001             Reached column 1?
; D 4118 A1 01 23       IFFALSEI XDA               No - carry on
; D 411B 11 01 00 03    LOADXI R1 0003             Reflect to 3
; D 411F 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000             and bounce - now heading right
; XDA:
; D 4123 50 50 0F       ADDXYZ R5 + R0 -> R15      This ball's row + the frame phase
; D 4126 2E 0F 09 60    READIDX R15 0960           Is this a frame for its vertical step?
; D 412A 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 412D A0 01 5A       IFTRUEI SYA                No - leave y alone this time
; D 4130 86 04 00 00    TESTXI R4 0000             Heading down?
; D 4134 A1 01 4B       IFFALSEI YUA               No - heading up
; D 4137 42 02          INCX R2                    y = y + 1
; D 4139 86 02 00 16    TESTXI R2 0016             Would the bottom edge pass line 23?
; D 413D A1 01 5A       IFFALSEI SYA               No - carry on
; D 4140 11 02 00 14    LOADXI R2 0014             Reflect to 20
; D 4144 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001             and bounce - now heading up
; D 4148 B0 01 5A       GAL SYA
; YUA:
; D 414B 43 02          DECX R2                    y = y - 1
; D 414D 8C 02          TESTXZ R2                  Reached line 0?
; D 414F A1 01 5A       IFFALSEI SYA               No - carry on
; D 4152 11 02 00 02    LOADXI R2 0002             Reflect to 2
; D 4156 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000             and bounce - now heading down
; SYA:
; D 415A 88 1B          TESTGXY R1 >= R11          Did x increase?
; D 415C A1 01 8A       IFFALSEI MLA               No - it moved left
; D 415F 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving right: the box starts at the old left edge
; D 4162 87 2C          TESTXY R2 = R12            Level?
; D 4164 A0 01 80       IFTRUEI RSA
; D 4167 88 2C          TESTGXY R2 >= R12          Down?
; D 4169 A1 01 76       IFFALSEI RUA               No - up
; D 416C 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Down: from the old top line
; D 416F 11 0F 0A B1    LOADXI R15 0AB1
; D 4173 B0 01 B2       GAL GOA
; RUA:
; D 4176 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13           Up: from the new top line
; D 4179 11 0F 0A 5E    LOADXI R15 0A5E
; D 417D B0 01 B2       GAL GOA
; RSA:
; D 4180 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 4183 11 0F 0A 8A    LOADXI R15 0A8A
; D 4187 B0 01 B2       GAL GOA
; MLA:
; D 418A 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 -> R14           Moving left: the box starts at the new left edge
; D 418D 87 2C          TESTXY R2 = R12            Level?
; D 418F A0 01 AB       IFTRUEI LSA
; D 4192 88 2C          TESTGXY R2 >= R12          Down?
; D 4194 A1 01 A1       IFFALSEI LUA               No - up
; D 4197 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Down: from the old top line
; D 419A 11 0F 0B 40    LOADXI R15 0B40
; D 419E B0 01 B2       GAL GOA
; LUA:
; D 41A1 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13           Up: from the new top line
; D 41A4 11 0F 0A DF    LOADXI R15 0ADF
; D 41A8 B0 01 B2       GAL GOA
; LSA:
; D 41AB 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 41AE 11 0F 0B 15    LOADXI R15 0B15
; GOA:
; D 41B2 BD 02 E6       CALL POSXY                 One cursor move
; D 41B5 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               The cells it left blanked, the cells it came to lit
; NRA:
; D 41B7 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11           Remember where this ball is
; D 41BA 23 00 7C       COPYXY R7 -> R12
; D 41BD 86 08 00 00    TESTXI R8 0000             Heading right?
; D 41C1 A1 01 D8       IFFALSEI XLB               No - heading left
; D 41C4 42 06          INCX R6                    x = x + 1
; D 41C6 86 06 00 4E    TESTXI R6 004E             Would the right edge pass column 79?
; D 41CA A1 01 E9       IFFALSEI XDB               No - carry on
; D 41CD 11 06 00 4C    LOADXI R6 004C             Reflect to 76
; D 41D1 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001             and bounce - now heading left
; D 41D5 B0 01 E9       GAL XDB
; XLB:
; D 41D8 43 06          DECX R6                    x = x - 1
; D 41DA 86 06 00 01    TESTXI R6 0001             Reached column 1?
; D 41DE A1 01 E9       IFFALSEI XDB               No - carry on
; D 41E1 11 06 00 03    LOADXI R6 0003             Reflect to 3
; D 41E5 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000             and bounce - now heading right
; XDB:
; D 41E9 50 A0 0F       ADDXYZ R10 + R0 -> R15     This ball's row + the frame phase
; D 41EC 2E 0F 09 60    READIDX R15 0960           Is this a frame for its vertical step?
; D 41F0 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 41F3 A0 02 20       IFTRUEI SYB                No - leave y alone this time
; D 41F6 86 09 00 00    TESTXI R9 0000             Heading down?
; D 41FA A1 02 11       IFFALSEI YUB               No - heading up
; D 41FD 42 07          INCX R7                    y = y + 1
; D 41FF 86 07 00 16    TESTXI R7 0016             Would the bottom edge pass line 23?
; D 4203 A1 02 20       IFFALSEI SYB               No - carry on
; D 4206 11 07 00 14    LOADXI R7 0014             Reflect to 20
; D 420A 11 09 00 01    LOADXI R9 0001             and bounce - now heading up
; D 420E B0 02 20       GAL SYB
; YUB:
; D 4211 43 07          DECX R7                    y = y - 1
; D 4213 8C 07          TESTXZ R7                  Reached line 0?
; D 4215 A1 02 20       IFFALSEI SYB               No - carry on
; D 4218 11 07 00 02    LOADXI R7 0002             Reflect to 2
; D 421C 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000             and bounce - now heading down
; SYB:
; D 4220 88 6B          TESTGXY R6 >= R11          Did x increase?
; D 4222 A1 02 50       IFFALSEI MLB               No - it moved left
; D 4225 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving right: the box starts at the old left edge
; D 4228 87 7C          TESTXY R7 = R12            Level?
; D 422A A0 02 46       IFTRUEI RSB
; D 422D 88 7C          TESTGXY R7 >= R12          Down?
; D 422F A1 02 3C       IFFALSEI RUB               No - up
; D 4232 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Down: from the old top line
; D 4235 11 0F 0A B1    LOADXI R15 0AB1
; D 4239 B0 02 78       GAL GOB
; RUB:
; D 423C 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13           Up: from the new top line
; D 423F 11 0F 0A 5E    LOADXI R15 0A5E
; D 4243 B0 02 78       GAL GOB
; RSB:
; D 4246 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 4249 11 0F 0A 8A    LOADXI R15 0A8A
; D 424D B0 02 78       GAL GOB
; MLB:
; D 4250 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 -> R14           Moving left: the box starts at the new left edge
; D 4253 87 7C          TESTXY R7 = R12            Level?
; D 4255 A0 02 71       IFTRUEI LSB
; D 4258 88 7C          TESTGXY R7 >= R12          Down?
; D 425A A1 02 67       IFFALSEI LUB               No - up
; D 425D 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Down: from the old top line
; D 4260 11 0F 0B 40    LOADXI R15 0B40
; D 4264 B0 02 78       GAL GOB
; LUB:
; D 4267 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13           Up: from the new top line
; D 426A 11 0F 0A DF    LOADXI R15 0ADF
; D 426E B0 02 78       GAL GOB
; LSB:
; D 4271 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 4274 11 0F 0B 15    LOADXI R15 0B15
; GOB:
; D 4278 BD 02 E6       CALL POSXY                 One cursor move
; D 427B C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               The cells it left blanked, the cells it came to lit
; NRB:
; D 427D 45 16          SUBXY R1 - R6              Close together after the move?
; D 427F 25             COPYMAA
; D 4280 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4282 11 0C 00 05    LOADXI R12 0005            Five
; D 4286 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12
; D 4288 A1 02 A7       IFFALSEI FAR               No - neither string touched the other ball
; D 428B 45 27          SUBXY R2 - R7
; D 428D 25             COPYMAA
; D 428E 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4290 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12
; D 4292 A1 02 A7       IFFALSEI FAR
; D 4295 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 -> R14           Close: one erase may have touched the other ball - draw both whole
; D 4298 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 429B BD 02 DB       CALL DRAW
; D 429E 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 -> R14
; D 42A1 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 42A4 BD 02 DB       CALL DRAW
; FAR:
; D 42A7 CC             SERST                      A key waiting?
; D 42A8 A1 02 C0       IFFALSEI NOKEY             No
; D 42AB CB             SERIN                      Read it
; D 42AC 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B                Was it ESC?
; D 42AF A1 02 C0       IFFALSEI NOKEY
; D 42B2 BD 02 C5       CALL KWAIT                 Yes: an arrow following?
; D 42B5 A1 03 04       IFFALSEI QUIT              No: ESC on its own stops it
; D 42B8 CB             SERIN                      an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 42B9 BD 02 C5       CALL KWAIT
; D 42BC A1 02 C0       IFFALSEI NOKEY
; D 42BF CB             SERIN
; NOKEY:
; D 42C0 C0 01          DLYI 01                    Pace the animation
; D 42C2 B0 00 9B       GAL LOOP                   Round again
; KWAIT:
; D 42C5 72 0B          PUSHX R11
; D 42C7 11 0B 00 08    LOADXI R11 0008
; KWAIT1:
; D 42CB CC             SERST
; D 42CC A0 02 D6       IFTRUEI KWAIT2
; D 42CF 43 0B          DECX R11
; D 42D1 8C 0B          TESTXZ R11
; D 42D3 A1 02 CB       IFFALSEI KWAIT1
; KWAIT2:
; D 42D6 73 0B          POPX R11
; D 42D8 CC             SERST                      Test: a key is waiting
; D 42D9 BE 00          RETURN
; DRAW:
; D 42DB BD 02 E6       CALL POSXY
; D 42DE 11 0F 0A 40    LOADXI R15 0A40
; D 42E2 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Reverse video, three rows of three, normal video
; D 42E4 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 42E6 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 42E8 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 42EA 2E 0D 09 80    READIDX R13 0980           Line: tens digit
; D 42EE C9             SEROUT
; D 42EF 2E 0D 09 E0    READIDX R13 09E0           units digit
; D 42F3 C9             SEROUT
; D 42F4 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'             ;
; D 42F6 2E 0E 09 80    READIDX R14 0980           Column: tens digit
; D 42FA C9             SEROUT
; D 42FB 2E 0E 09 E0    READIDX R14 09E0           units digit
; D 42FF C9             SEROUT
; D 4300 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'             H
; D 4302 BE 00          RETURN
; QUIT:
; D 4304 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4306 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4308 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F '?'             ?
; D 430A CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 430C CA 35          SEROUTI 35 '5'             5
; D 430E CA 68          SEROUTI 68 'h'             h - show the cursor again
; D 4310 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4312 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4314 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 4316 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A 'J'             J
; D 4318 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 431A CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 431C CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'             H - cursor home
; D 431E F0 00 00       BREAK                      End of program

